  "term": "butyrylcholinesterase",
  "definition": "Butyrylcholinesterase is an enzyme involved in reducing the activity of a neurotransmitter. In the context of neurological disorders such as Alzheimer’s disease, increased butyrylcholinesterase activity or levels are associated with disease progression.",
